Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"bernadette|Tom. Good. Neighborhood Watch Captain, potluck committee chair. Forty RSVPs. Thirty-nine dishes. One bread guy.":"","tom|Did you call the gas company?":"","bernadette|Every pilot light on 2nd Avenue went out at noon. Every one. Including mine. I had a casserole IN there.":"","tnb|Wow. Okay. Big mood, buddy.":"","tnb|Okay. Up. Everybody up. Hot cocoa later. Lots of it.":"","tom|You can fix anything.":"","tnb|I can fix most things. I fixed your dishwasher with a butter knife.":"","skeeter|Wooooo. Pfft. Pfft. Pfft. That was me. I blew them all out. Every stove on the block.":"","tom|A note taped inside the lid: FOR THE NEXT SHIFT. HAVE A GOOD RUN. BOOKER W.":"","tnb|Babe, close a door on it. Any door.":"","tnb|Under hero.":"","tnb|Babe. BABE. We turned a turntable. Do you know how many people get to turn a turntable? Like eleven.":"","tom|You took every pilot light on 2nd Avenue.":"","tnb|Okay. Up. Everybody up. That was hot. That was SO hot.":"","tom|Give the flames back. No touching, please.":"","bigone|...Forty? Nobody has asked me for forty anything since 1963. Bring the dough.":"","tnb|Noted, Bernadette.":"","tnb|You know what tonight was, babe? Toast.":"","tom|It works on one level. Barely.":"","michael|Best potluck ever. Lachlan fell asleep in the bread basket.":"","washington|My daddy drove the 7 line out of the old Car Barn. He said the stove down there could warm a whole street.":"","mudling|Nobody ever finishes me. They pour me, they get busy, they forget.":"","mudling|Round 2. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 3. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 4. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|Round 5. Still lukewarm.":"","mudling|...somebody made me and walked away.":"","mudling|I was hot once. For about four minutes.":"","mudling|Everybody brings me home. Nobody ever opens me again.":"","mudling|Reheated! Round two!":"","mudling|Round 2. Day 2 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 3. Day 3 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 4. Day 4 in the fridge.":"","mudling|Round 5. Day 5 in the fridge.":"","mudling|...I was a lasagna. I think. Once.":"","log|They used to throw me over the sparks when the welders worked. I put out every fire in this barn.":"","log|Round 2. Still damp.":"","log|Round 3. Still damp.":"","log|Round 4. Still damp.":"","log|...why bother. Why bother at all.":"","log|Every spark in here, I put it out. Somebody has to.":"","skeeter|I blew out every pilot light on 2nd Avenue. Pfft. Pfft. Pfft. Very satisfying.":"","skeeter|Woooo! Round two!":"","log|Round 5. Still damp.":"","skeeter|Round 2. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Still drafty.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Still drafty.":"","log|Why bother? Round two.":"","toad|Ironbelly used to warm every lunch in here. Now everything is cold, and everything is EW.":"","toad|Ew! Round two!":"","toad|Round 2. Still not eating it.":"","toad|Round 3. Still not eating it.":"","toad|Round 4. Still not eating it.":"","toad|I only eat the crust. No, the middle. No. Neither.":"","bigone|Biscuits for the night crew. Cornbread on Fridays. Every night from 1912 to 1963.":"","bigone|Everybody has a little fire upstairs. I only borrowed it.":"","bigone|Stoke it! Round two!":"","bigone|Round 2. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 3. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 4. Still preheating.":"","bigone|Round 5. Still preheating.":"","bigone|...cold. Sixty years cold.":"","bigone|Nobody bakes anything anymore. Not in me.":"","sal|Airport? You JUST landed. Your young man said, and I quote, \"forty loaves, babe.\"":"","log|...Oh. Visitors. Great. I suppose you want that little flame.":"","tnb|Okay. Burner one. Burner two. Burner three. Righty tighty. Lefty... no, righty. Righty tighty.":"","tnb|On the day of the POTLUCK, though.":"","toad|Round 5. Still not eating it.":"","grace|Number eight is in Los Angeles. Call me BEFORE you touch it. I sharpened the pencil.":"","bernadette|3468. You're back. Don't touch that. It's on my street.":"","tnb|Welcome home. Don't open the salad spinner. That's loaf thirty-one.":"","grace|Tata. Did you touch it?":"","bigone|Shut that door. You're letting the cold in.":"","bernadette|8:42 this morning. White sedan, parked across the Washington driveway for four minutes. Rental. Airport lot sticker on the windshield. I have the plate.":"","deedee|The drawer is ready for number eight. Also, a fancy letter came for you from the Moon Club. That place has been locked since 1971. I did not open it.":"","washington|Tom! Get out here and look at my roses!":"","odette|Tom! My gumbo's been on since six, and right now it's the temperature of a handshake.":"","olivia|That's my dog under the table, and I've never seen that loaf before in my life.":"","carmen|My griddle is cold. Do you know what a pupusa is off a cold griddle? It's an apology.":"","log|Stop right there. Somebody's had a fire going in this building, and I'm putting an end to it.":"","toad|What's in the salad spinner? Is that sourdough? No. Too sour.":"","tnb|Bready Mercury was climbing out of the crock at five this morning. I wasn't going to argue with him.":"","grace|How big?":"","bigone|Fifty years I fed the night crews out of this room. Then one morning in 1963 they shut off my gas and chained the door, and not one of them said a word to me about it.":"","bernadette|One man. Long coat, in this heat. He pointed something at the roses, there was a flash, and when I could see again, there was that.":"","deedee|I held it up to the lamp. There's a piano on it.":"","rose|Why didn't he jump?":"","washington|And the red's gone out of everything around it. The roses, the lawn, my good hose. All grey.":"","odette|You're following them with a salad spinner.":"","olivia|She can get in line. She owes me a couch.":"","carmen|And this one is drinking purple soda before noon.":"","log|First it's one little flame. Then it's music. Then people have friends over. I've seen where it goes.":"","toad|That makes it worse. Do you have it in white? With the crusts cut off?":"","tnb|So we bring twenty-four and tell Bernadette it's a tasting menu.":"","grace|That's bigger than the golf cart. And it's in Los Angeles. I said Los Angeles.":"","bigone|I've seen your stoves. A flame the size of a pea, burning all day and all night so somebody can boil one egg. I'm putting them to work.":"","bernadette|Then something small and on fire picked a gold thing up off the sidewalk and ran toward the boulevard. I wrote it down as a raccoon. I know it wasn't a raccoon.":"","deedee|Your father says he once baked sixty loaves in one morning. He has never baked.":"","rose|I'm going to be number one.":"","washington|You're the one who's always on a plane, Tom. Did you bring this home with you?":"","skeeter|No, he didn't. There's no draft in here.":"","odette|Go on, then. And Tom, if my gumbo isn't hot by six, I'm telling Bernadette it was your idea.":"","olivia|He's got it.":"","carmen|No. Is it cold?":"","log|Then I got here just in time.":"","toad|I tried. It was too hot. Before that it was too cold. I'd like to speak to whoever packed me.":"","tom|I promise. I packed a ruler.":"","tnb|She came by at seven to check on us. She called me the Other Tom and said my bowls were too close together.":"","grace|Thank you. Who's the lady behind you with the clipboard?":"","bigone|And they're no good. Every flame on the street, and I still can't get warm. A fire's no use with nothing to bake.":"","bernadette|Write that down and sign it. Nobody on this street ever does.":"","washington|Seven. And it never once came up at a block meeting.":"","skeeter|It's an old building. They all do this. Have you tried a sweater?":"","odette|Bernadette, your diagram had my gumbo behind the paper plates.":"","olivia|Tom. A rosebush got sealed in orange glass, every stove on the block went out, and it was all fixed by six. I'd love a quote.":"","carmen|Everyone got it. Then we moved the table.":"","log|Fine. Have your fun. Keep it down after ten.":"","toad|I'm still not eating the crust.":"","tom|You started without me. I made a schedule on the plane. It has tabs.":"","tnb|I said, 'Great note, Bernadette.' Then she stood there waiting for me to move them, and I opened a soda.":"","grace|I'm Grace. I'm nine. I keep the chart.":"","bigone|I don't take bread from a man holding a salad spinner.":"","bernadette|He was here fifteen minutes before your cab, 3468. You'd have seen him yourself if you were ever home.":"","skeeter|I'm not holding anything. That flame was like that when I got here.":"","odette|Thirty-eight thousand dollars, and the porch was already crooked.":"","olivia|That's a quote. I'm using it.":"","tom|Forty loaves, two at a time, forty-five minutes each. That's fifteen hours of oven, and we have nine.":"","tnb|It was a long soda.":"","grace|A person! I said it was a person. What kind of car? What time? Did anybody get the license plate?":"","bigone|Too wet. Who taught you to shape a loaf?":"","bernadette|Chained since 1963. I have the key. Nobody has ever asked me for it.":"","washington|The only thing at the end of the boulevard is the old Car Barn. My father drove the night streetcar out of it.":"","skeeter|I'll be back in the winter. I always am.":"","tom|She'll count them. She counted the folding chairs at Mr. Washington's birthday.":"","tnb|I've seen this movie, you know. The lady who runs the potluck always has something in her basement.":"","grace|Tata, I like her.":"","bigone|Better. Cut the top deeper next time. It needs somewhere to go.":"","bernadette|Then she can run the block meeting, because she'd be the first person on this street to keep a promise.":"","washington|If this turns out to be a parking meter, I'm going to be upset.":"","tom|What did you tell her?":"","tnb|Two padlocks. On a shed.":"","grace|The gold coin is with the biggest thing that woke up. Find it, put it in the hole, and call me when the color comes back.":"","bigone|Hm. That one's a loaf.":"","bernadette|Who's asking?":"","washington|'Trim to regulation height.' Bernadette, you taped a notice to my roses.":"","tom|How long did she wait?":"","tnb|I'm going to stand over here, on the part of the sidewalk that still has a color.":"","grace|That's new. I need a new color for fire.":"","bigone|That's the first bread out of me since 1963. Don't stand there looking at it. Cut it.":"","bernadette|White sedan. 8:42. Yes.":"","washington|It was inside a block all day.":"","tom|She doesn't have a basement. She has that shed with the two padlocks.":"","tnb|That's what I don't like about it. The dough rises. The dog jumps. That thing is just waiting.":"","grace|The man rented a car AT THE AIRPORT. That means he flies back and forth. Like you. The next one is here. Come home.":"","bigone|I know what it is. It's my pension. Sixty years late, and a little flame carried it in this morning.":"","bernadette|Give the niece my number, 3468. And don't get ideas. I'm not being friendly. She keeps records, and I respect records.":"","washington|Hold on. This is the Car Barn loaf. My father brought one home every morning until they shut that place. Who baked this?":"","tom|That's your whole rosebush. It's inside an orange block the size of a minivan.":"","tnb|Is that the chart? It has a key. It's color coded. That's the wall the detective has right before they take his badge away.":"","bigone|So it's not even mine.":"","bernadette|Nineteen years I've carried this key. You're welcome in advance, since I won't hear it afterwards.":"","washington|Well, he took his time about it. You know, in 1979, when I bought that house...":"","tom|No, sir. But I've seen seven of them, and I know how to open one.":"","tnb|There are two of them now.":"","bigone|Sixty years, and the first gold through that door belongs to a shrub.":"","bernadette|Don't be smart, Other Tom.":"","washington|I'm glad somebody on this street listens.":"","tom|They don't do anything. They just sit there.":"","tnb|I watch a lot of scary movies. That was good, though. Top ten.":"","bigone|What time is this potluck?":"","bernadette|Forty loaves. Six o'clock. I don't care what's in there.":"","tom|Mr. Washington, there's a notice taped to your roses in there.":"","tnb|Through the dog door. Nara's never once used the dog door.":"","bigone|How many loaves?":"","bernadette|At 5:30 this morning. Before the incident. It still applies.":"","tom|You saw a person do this?":"","tnb|Then I guess we're following a flame down the street. Bring the dough. I'm not leaving loaf thirty-one alone with the dog.":"","bigone|I used to do two hundred before midnight. Load me. If this is my last shift, I'm not ending it on three.":"","bernadette|The date's on it.":"","tom|Bernadette, that's the most useful thing anyone has told me in eight of these.":"","tnb|It's grape. Do you want one?":"","bigone|Somebody's going to stand up tonight and say they arranged this bread. Somebody always did.":"","bernadette|That bulb is evidence, 3468.":"","tom|Before I touch anything, I have to make a phone call. I promised a nine-year-old.":"","tnb|It's the only thing on this street that's the right temperature.":"","bigone|Take your shrub money. And shut my door on the way out. I'd like to cool down slowly.":"","bernadette|Then I want it logged first.":"","tom|I did not touch it. Look. Round hole, burnt bulb, grey patch.":"","bernadette|Thirty-eight. Thirty-nine. That's thirty-nine, 3468. I said forty.":"","tom|A minivan.":"","tnb|Chained from the outside since 1963. You lock a building to keep people out. You chain it to keep something in.":"","bernadette|The dog owes this street a loaf.":"","tom|Grace, somebody saw a man do this one. He came in a rental car.":"","tnb|Oh, we're going in. I just want it on the record that I knew.":"","bernadette|Hot dishes on the left. Everyone got the diagram.":"","tom|I know. They're going to start a newsletter.":"","tnb|Tom. That's a turntable. They used to spin a whole streetcar on that.":"","bernadette|If I could have your attention. The Watch would like to thank the Watch for arranging the bread.":"","tom|It ran toward the boulevard, and it was on fire.":"","tnb|I need about an hour. But go ahead.":"","tom|Our pilot light just walked out of the house.":"","tnb|It's a wet blanket. I'm not making a joke. Look at it.":"","tom|We have forty loaves of raw dough and no fire.":"","tnb|Hi. We can hear you.":"","tom|Every flame on the block walked out. We're following them.":"","tnb|You've got a flame in there. You could warm something up.":"","tom|It's loaf thirty-one.":"","tnb|Three flames, one motor. On set I once fixed a zipper with a paper clip while the actor was still walking. This thing's holding still.":"","tom|So we're not going in?":"","tnb|It says Boiler Room. I'm just reading it out loud so we both know.":"","tom|Do you need a minute?":"","tnb|No, you go. You're the one who's polite to things.":"","tom|That blanket is talking, and it's soaking wet.":"","tnb|He's got a point about the egg.":"","tom|We're having forty people over at six.":"","tnb|Forty.":"","tom|Did you feel that?":"","tnb|We know exactly who.":"","tom|You're holding one of our flames.":"","tnb|Okay. Now I'll stand on the lawn.":"","tom|You sound exactly like my first landlord.":"","tnb|He called it.":"","tom|The starter is nine years old and it has a name.":"","tnb|I figured. Take a loaf for your mom.":"","tom|Nara, this is what you sound like.":"","tnb|We're fine. She thinks I moved the bowls.":"","tom|After you.":"","tom|That oven is the size of our kitchen, and every flame on the block is inside it.":"","tom|Those flames belong to the stoves on 2nd Avenue.":"","tom|We have dough.":"","tom|There's a gold coin on your door. I need it, and I have to tell you what it does before I take it.":"","tom|It isn't your pension. It opens an orange block on our street. When it does, every flame goes home and you go back to being an oven. A cold one. You won't be able to talk.":"","tom|No. It has a rosebush on it.":"","tom|Six o'clock.":"","tom|Thank you for the bread.":"","tom|It goes in the round hole. It's your rosebush, so it should be you.":"","tom|It's going in my mother's junk drawer with the other seven.":"","tom|No comment.":"","tom|Somebody always did.":"","tom|An old-timer from the barn. He retired today.":"","tom|I have to fly back tomorrow.":"","tom|That leaves you alone on this street with Bernadette.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"grace":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"JVVJ6VsnUPJAdfGmEBGP","name":"AoT Grace (Gretchen)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"deedee":{"voice_id":"3atomJkX2UWSHPSg86Z0","name":"AoT Deedee (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":false},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"amy":{"voice_id":"HLSHrV3D7Gp6sEFcHNev","name":"AoT Amy (Kind)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"heavy Long Island accent","designed":false},"boomie":{"voice_id":"FgGtmhYdBou3a14mKYgx","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a big, warm, rich singer’s voice, bubbly and motherly, slides into song mid-sentence, laughs from the belly. Clean studio recording."},"bean":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late twenties with an upbeat, rambling, friendly American voice. A little scattered, quick bursts of words, cheerful and unbothered. Light and bright. Clean studio recording."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"pistachio":{"voice_id":"LyoSZrqTSG25l7i0uBGl","name":"AoT Mr. Pistachio","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late fifties with a warm, hearty Long Island New York accent, an ice cream shop owner who loves his regulars, booming friendly laugh, talks with his hands, a little dramatic about his scoops. Clean studio recording."},"brainfreeze":{"voice_id":"kYM9iwUI7t87mhAOBs1T","name":"AoT Brain Freeze","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon villain who is a walking chest freezer: a flat, cold, humming monotone with a slight metallic buzz, deadpan and sulky, slow and heavy, with a lonely sadness underneath that cracks through when he is surprised. Animated character voice."},"boomie2":{"voice_id":"rrjdoujYPDo3FGeRqm3Q","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young Black American woman in her late thirties to early fourties with a warm, rich, low alto voice, smooth and a little husky, deeper than most women’s voices. A gospel and soul singer, kind and bubbly, laughs from the belly, slides into song mid-sentence. Clean studio recording."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"justin":{"voice_id":"Pp9gl3BrnVq62dIWU2sx","name":"AoT Justin (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his early forties with an easygoing, friendly voice, Long Island born with a slight country twang. Goofy proud dad, handyman, sports fan, relaxed and warm, quick to laugh. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."}});
